# Owner login of the staging database, for the one-off jobs only (Pass 37): Compose gives
# it to `migrate`, `backup` and `check` (db-verify), never to the app, the worker or the
# scheduler (deploy/staging/compose.yaml, x-owner-env). Copy to
# deploy/staging/staging-owner.env (git-ignored, mode 600, root-owned on the host) from the
# owner credential's own secret — not the app's env secret (RELEASE_READINESS_DECISIONS.md
# R-4). It must be the login that OWNS the database objects (DATABASE_ROLES.md § 5), not the
# managed-database master user. Every value below is a placeholder.
OWNER_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://flexibx_owner:CHANGE_ME@staging-db.example.internal:5432/flexibx_staging?sslmode=require
